     1	"""V2 Native Edge-Proof — post-hoc replay outcome miner.
     2	
     3	Maintains an incremental price + bundle store on disk so the
     4	edge-proof evaluator has real future-outcome windows (1m / 5m / 15m /
     5	1h) to score against. Each invocation:
     6	
     7	1. Appends the current ``v2:market:prices:{symbol}`` snapshot to a
     8	   per-symbol price-timeline JSONL.
     9	2. Appends new shadow / paper-intent rows from ``v2:paper:ledger``
    10	   into a replay-bundles JSONL store (deduplicating by intent_id).
    11	3. For each existing bundle, attempts to fill any outcome window that
    12	   now has enough elapsed time and at least one timeline point on or
    13	   after the window endpoint. Windows that still cannot be filled stay
    14	   `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`.
    15	4. Computes after-cost return, max favorable, max adverse, fee drag,
    16	   slippage estimate per filled window.
    17	5. Assigns objective labels from realized after-cost outcome + paper
    18	   gate decision. The miner NEVER fabricates outcomes; missing windows
    19	   stay explicit.
    20	
    21	Safety:
    22	
    23	- Reads only ``v2:*`` Redis keys via the safe reader and the
    24	  V2-vs-legacy comparator public mirror.
    25	- Writes only under
    26	  ``claude_worklog/final_readiness/v2_post_hoc_replay_outcome_miner/`` and
    27	  ``v2/frontend/public/v2_post_hoc_replay_outcome_miner/``.
    28	- Never modifies legacy code, never calls the exchange, never enables
    29	  live trading, never adopts symbols, never creates approval markers.
    30	"""
